  "proposal": {
    "customer_job": "A finance reviewer asks the Clock Test employee for an accounts-receivable aging answer: per-invoice outstanding balance, overdue flag and days overdue, plus known subtotals, to decide which customers to chase and at which dunning stage (30/60/90+ days).",
    "consequence": "Hypothetical: a wrong day count across month or year boundaries moves an invoice into the wrong aging bucket (premature escalation or a missed 90-day collection step); a cent error in non-round subtraction or summation misstates what is chased; flagging a paid-in-full past-due invoice as overdue chases a customer who owes nothing. Exposure unknown.",
    "hypothesis": "Hypothetical regression: the employee may misapply the fixed reconciliation rules for aging boundaries.",
